## Key Learnings

* Baselines must be **entity-specific** and **robust** (quantiles over means) to avoid false-positive inflation
* Peer grouping and time awareness are essential for meaningful “normal” behavior definitions
* Detection quality improves more from **context enrichment and alert hygiene** than from stricter thresholds
* Architectures must support feedback loops; otherwise detection logic decays over time

